+"""Verified generator for Mod/Resc Boolean-matrix factorizations.
+
+The source is arXiv:1002.1292.  Section 2 defines the asymmetric Boolean
+product C = M tensor R, and Theorem 1 identifies a k-column factorization
+with a k-biclique edge cover of the bipartite graph whose bi-adjacency
+matrix is C.
+
+This generator samples two collections of circular intervals on a hidden
+cycle.  Their incidence vectors are the rows of M and R, so C is computed
+directly and the factor pair is known without solving C.  The row and column
+orders are random and only C is shown.  A generic implementation of the
+paper's maximal-biclique algorithm is measured separately from several
+in-context attacks.
