+This is a native exact family based on [Nor et al., *Mod/Resc Parsimony Inference* (arXiv:1002.1292)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1002.1292). The solver receives the paper's Boolean compatibility matrix (C), with labelled rows and columns in independently shuffled presentation order, and must give affine triples defining Boolean Mod and rescue matrices (M,R). The checker expands the triples and recomputes every entry of the paper's asymmetric product (C=M\otimes R). It also constructs a fooling set of size (k) and checks its diagonal and cross-entries exactly, so the claimed width is certified minimal rather than merely feasible.
 
