The result obtained on the {\it Culex pipiens}
dataset indicates that $8$ pairs of mod/resc genes are required to explain the
dataset. This appear to be in sharp contrast to more simple patterns
seen in other host
species~\cite{Mercot2004,Dobson2001,Bordenstein2007}
that had led to the general belief that cytoplasmic incompatibility
can be explained with a single pair of mod / resc genes. In biological
terms, this result means that contrary to earlier beliefs, the number
of genetic determinants of cytoplasmic incompatibility present in a
single {\it Wolbachia} strain can be large, consistent with the view that it
might involve repeated genetic elements such as transposable elements
or phages. \\\\\\


