The corrected rerun reached the same substantive conclusion through the named ladder and the first custom escalation, then the shared OpenRouter key hit its total spending limit during the next rung. Because the required three-escalation bar had already been defeated and the compact certificate stayed far below every output cap, this is an H failure on Track B—not a cap-bound paper. I’m documenting that rejection and retaining the built module under the required `rejected_gen_...` name.
