codex
The paper was correctly rejected: the attempted family fails H on Track B.

Both oracle vendors repeatedly solved the affine-moment construction through all named presets and a custom escalation. Increasing size only repeated the same recoverable calculation. G and V passed, but hardness did not.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.1292/REJECTED.md) — full decision, theorem references, mechanical cost, compact-route length, and oracle evidence.
- [rejected_gen_1002_1292.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.1292/rejected_gen_1002_1292.py) — retained attempted generator, as required.
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.1292/README.md) — audit summary and caveats.
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.1292/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl) — corrected hardening attempts.
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.1292/selftest_report.json) — G1–G9 construction/checker measurements.

Final G1 regression: 16/16 planted certificates verified. The shared OpenRouter key exhausted during a later rung, but only after the required three-escalation rejection threshold had already been defeated. The stale script-owned `.meta.json` verdict is explicitly documented and should not be treated as a genuine `cap_bound`.

Source: [Nor et al., Mod/Resc Parsimony Inference](https://arxiv.org/abs/1002.1292).
